.TH LIST 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Value Types"
.SH NAME
list \- built-in list value type methods
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists in y-- are ordered, mutable sequences that can hold elements of any type.
.SH "CORE METHODS"
.TP
\fBappend(val)\fR -> list()
Appends \fBval\fR to the end of the list.
.TP
\fBget(index, [default_return])\fR -> any
Returns the element at \fBindex\fR. Supports negative indices (e.g., -1 is the last element).
If out of bounds, returns \fBdefault_return\fR if provided, else None.
.TP
\fBinsert(index, val)\fR -> list()
Inserts \fBval\fR before the element at \fBindex\fR.
.TP
\fBpop([index])\fR -> any
Removes and returns the element at \fBindex\fR. If no index is provided, pops the last element.
.TP
\fBremove(val)\fR -> none()
Removes the first occurrence of \fBval\fR. Throws ValueError if not found.
.TP
\fBclear()\fR -> list()
Removes all elements from the list.
.TP
\fBextend(iterable)\fR -> list()
Appends all elements from another list, set, or range.
.SH "SEARCHING & SORTING"
.TP
\fBcount(val)\fR -> int()
Returns the number of occurrences of \fBval\fR.
.TP
\fBindex(val)\fR -> int()
Returns the first index of \fBval\fR, or -1 if not found.
.TP
\fBreverse([modify_original, custom_lambda])\fR -> list()
Reverses the list in place.
.TP
\fBsort([reverse_sort, modify_original, custom_lambda])\fR -> list()
Sorts the list.
.TP
\fBshuffle()\fR -> list()
Randomly shuffles the elements in place.
.SH "MATH & AGGREGATION"
.TP
\fBsum() / min() / max() / average()\fR
Performs mathematical aggregations on numeric lists. min() and max() work on strings too.
.SH "UTILITIES"
.TP
\fBflatten()\fR -> list()
Recursively flattens nested lists.
.TP
\fBchunk(size)\fR -> list()
Splits the list into smaller sub-lists of \fBsize\fR.
.TP
\fBrotate(n)\fR -> list()
Rotates elements by \fBn\fR positions.
.TP
\fBunique()\fR -> list()
Removes duplicates.
.TP
\fBjoin([sep=""])\fR -> string()
Joins elements into a string.
.TP
\fBfill(val, [count])\fR -> list()
Fills the list with copies of \fBval\fR.
.SH "HEAP OPERATIONS"
.TP
\fBMaxHeapify() / MinHeapify()\fR -> list()
Converts the list into a max-heap or min-heap.
.TP
\fBMaxHeapPop() / MinHeapPop()\fR -> any
Pops the root element of the heap.
.TP
\fBMaxHeapPush(val) / MinHeapPush(val)\fR -> list()
Pushes \fBval\fR onto the heap.
.SH "FUNCTIONAL METHODS"
.TP
\fBAll_Of / Any_Of / None_Of / One_Of (lambda)\fR -> bool()
Boolean aggregations.
.TP
\fBselect / reject (lambda)\fR -> list()
Filters elements.
.TP
\fBmap(lambda)\fR -> list()
Maps elements.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tuple(3), set(3)
